# Cline Rules for Patrimio

Read AI_RULES.md in project root before any task.

## Quick reference

- Stack: Next.js 15 + Supabase + shadcn/ui + Vercel
- DB: Remote only (no Docker), `npm run db:push`, `npm run db:types`
- Money: INTEGER cents always (`850.75€ → 85075`)
- Auth: JWT from `supabase.auth.getUser()`, never from body
- i18n: `useTranslations()` mandatory, no hardcoded strings
- Tests: Vitest (unit) + Playwright (E2E, iPhone 14)
- Security: RLS + Zod `.strict()` + soft delete + signed URLs

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev          # Dev server
npm run type-check   # TypeScript validation
npm run test         # Vitest unit tests
npm run test:e2e     # Playwright E2E
npm run db:push      # Apply migrations (remote)
npm run db:types     # Regenerate types (remote)
```

## Agent delegation

- Any task → `@project-orchestrator` (analyzes + executes)
- Full feature → `@feature-builder` (DB+API+UI+tests)
- DB schema → `@db-architect`
- Security audit → `@security-reviewer`
- Code review → `@code-reviewer`

## Critical paths

- Migrations: `supabase/migrations/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_name.sql`
- Types: `types/database.ts` (generated, never edit)
- API: `app/api/**/route.ts`
- Financial: `lib/financial/formatters.ts`
- i18n: `messages/es.json`, `messages/en.json`

## Anti-patterns

❌ Edit `types/database.ts` manually
❌ Use `parseFloat` for money
❌ Hardcode UI strings
❌ Physical DELETE on tables
❌ API routes without Zod validation
❌ Tables without RLS
❌ Assume file content (read first)
